          "reviewed_on": "2026-11-07",
          "notes": "The public bobyqa_module::bobyqa minimizes a smooth real scalar function under lower/upper variable bounds without supplied derivatives. It builds quadratic interpolation models and uses a trust-region method, dispatching to private BOBYQB. The selected public interface has ten arguments: N,NPT,X,XL,XU,RHOBEG,RHOEND,IPRINT,MAXFUN,CALFUN; it allocates workspace internally. This differs from older external BOBYQA interfaces with a user workspace and from other forks with status/F outputs. N must be at least 2; N+2<=NPT<=(N+1)*(N+2)/2; NPT=2*N+1 is a suggested initial choice. Provide conforming REAL(wp) vectors X/XL/XU of length at least N. wp is REAL64 in the pinned kind_module. Require positive RHOEND<=RHOBEG and each bound interval at least 2*RHOBEG wide; scale variables appropriately. The wrapper can adjust the initial X away from bounds to construct its interpolation model. CALFUN(N,X,F) is a subroutine callback with default INTEGER N, assumed-shape REAL(wp) X(:) INTENT(IN), and scalar REAL(wp) F INTENT(OUT). X is overwritten by the best estimate; neither objective value nor convergence status is an output argument. Reevaluate the callback to obtain F and independently assess the result. Invalid NPT or insufficient bound spacing prints a diagnostic and returns; normal return alone is not a success certificate. IPRINT=0 suppresses ordinary iteration output but not those wrapper diagnostics. MAXFUN limits callback evaluations; there is no public counter/status result. This review inspects the public wrapper, callback declarations and precision selection, not every private interpolation/trust-region kernel. The illustrative calling program was not compiled or run for this independent review. The existing playground box-quadratic checked driver remains separately recorded and is not reclassified as a new independent numerical test.",
